IMPORTANT: Read this Agreement before installing or using the Software.


Article 0. Acceptance

(1) You agree to all terms of the version of this Agreement specified below
    (identified by the version number and effective date at the top of this
    file), at the time specified below. If you do not agree, do not install,
    obtain, or use the Software.
      (i)   If you use the installer: the version displayed during installation,
            when you indicate acceptance.
      (ii)  If you do not use the installer (for example, when you use the
            source code from the public repository, or fork it in order to make
            an Improvement Proposal): the version included with the Software
            when you obtain it (including by downloading, git clone, or forking)
            or first use it.
      (iii) If you install a newer release of the Software (by installing over
            an existing installation, updating, or the like): the version
            displayed or included at that time, when you install it.

(2) If you are a minor, install and use the Software only with the consent of a
    parent or legal guardian. Use of the Software may incur usage-based charges
    from third-party services (Article 8 (1)). Where a third-party service used
    by the Software (such as Google AI Studio (Gemini API) or Fish Audio) has
    age or other eligibility requirements, you must comply with them (Article 3
    (2)).


Article 1. Definitions

(1) "Software" means all files contained in this distribution package and in the
    source code repository published by the Author
    (ChordDotE/watashinosekaito_hatsunemiku on GitHub), including source code,
    configuration files, documentation, and image files.

(2) "Personal Use" means use by a natural person for private purposes, which is
    neither Commercial Use (3) nor Business Use (4).

(3) "Commercial Use" means use of the Software by a natural person, in a manner
    that is not Business Use (4), to obtain, directly or indirectly, money or
    any other economic benefit. This includes, without limitation, monetized
    streaming or posting.

(4) "Business Use" means any use of the Software by a business (a corporation,
    organization, or sole proprietor, including non-profit organizations), and
    any use of the Software for the purposes of a business by anyone, WHETHER OR
    NOT ANY PAYMENT IS INVOLVED. This includes providing services relating to
    the Software to others, such as installation support or hosting servers
    that run the Software. However, a natural person monetizing his or her own
    streams or posts is treated as Commercial Use (3), not as Business Use.

(5) "Adaptation" means creating software having equivalent or similar
    functionality based on the contents of the Software. This includes manual
    reimplementation, automated translation, and generation using large language
    models or other machine learning.

(6) "Author" means ChordDotE, who created the Software and licenses it under
    this Agreement. Contact details are set out in Article 7.

(7) "Modified Version" means the Software, in whole or in part, with
    modifications. This includes material consisting only of the modified
    portions, and diffs.

(8) "Improvement Proposal" means showing modifications to the Author, for the
    purpose of improving the Software, so that the Author can decide whether to
    adopt them. This includes GitHub pull requests and diffs attached to issues.


Article 2. Ownership of Rights

(1) What belongs to the Author.
    All copyright and other intellectual property rights in the Software (the
    source code, prompts, configuration files, documentation, image files, and
    other files in the Software) belong to the Author, except for
    the third-party items listed in (2). However,
    the portions of the Software that depict the character Hatsune Miku are a
    derivative work under the Piapro Character License; the character itself
    belongs to a third party as stated in (2).

(2) What does NOT belong to the Author (third-party rights).
    The following are not included in the Software, and the Author holds no
    rights in them. They belong to their respective rights holders, and are
    obtained or configured by you (see Articles 3 and 13):

      - the character Hatsune Miku (Crypton Future Media, Inc. and others);
      - Live2D models and the Cubism SDK (Live2D Inc. and others);
      - Fish Audio and other voice synthesis software,
        services, and voice models;
      - third-party dependency libraries; and
      - scores, audio, and other material that the Software downloads from the
        internet in its music features.

    However, a few files taken from third-party dependency libraries are
    included in the Software. Each such file belongs to the copyright holder
    stated in it and is governed by the license stated in it.

(3) What is generated with the Software.
    The Author claims no rights in the conversations, text, music, singing, or
    other output you generate with the Software. However, portions derived from
    an original work or other third-party material remain subject to that third
    party's rights (Article 8 (6)).

(4) This Agreement licenses use of the Software within the scope set out in it;
    it does not transfer any right to you. All rights not expressly granted here
    are reserved by the Author. The restrictions in this Agreement apply to
    users; they do not restrict the Author's own use, modification,
    publication, or distribution of the Software.

(5) Modification for your own environment under Article 4 (2), and making an
    Improvement Proposal under Article 4 (6), do not change the rights described
    in this Article.

(6) The Author decides freely whether to adopt an Improvement Proposal. A person
    who makes an Improvement Proposal grants the Author, free of charge and
    without limitation in time or territory, the right to incorporate its
    contents into the Software, modify them, and publish and distribute them
    under this Agreement or other terms set by the Author, and shall not
    exercise moral rights against the Author. The Software including adopted
    contents is governed by this Agreement.


Article 3. Scope

(1) This Agreement applies to the Software. It does NOT apply to the following,
    which are governed by the terms of their respective providers:
      - Google AI Studio (Gemini API) (Google's terms);
      - Fish Audio services and voice models;
      - voice synthesis models generally (no voice model is included in the
        Software; the choice of model is left to the user and is governed by
        that model's provider);
      - Tavily (when web search is used), Cloudflare (when external access is
        used), and other third-party services used by the Software (each
        provider's terms);
      - VOCALOID6 and Hatsune Miku V6 (when the music features are used;
        purchased separately by the user and governed by their providers'
        licenses);
      - Live2D models and the Cubism SDK (not included in the Software;
        obtained by the user from the official distributor);
      - the Hatsune Miku character (rights of Crypton Future Media, Inc. and
        others); and
      - third-party dependency libraries (each under its own license, including
        the files described in the proviso to Article 2 (2)).

(2) Your use of third-party services and software used by the Software (such as
    Google AI Studio (Gemini API), Fish Audio, Tavily, Cloudflare, Gmail, and
    VOCALOID6) is based on your own agreement with each provider. You must
    comply with their respective terms (including age and other eligibility
    requirements). The Author is not responsible for whether your use complies
    with those terms, for the suspension or change of those services or
    software, for their fees, or for anything that occurs on the side of those
    services or software (except in cases of the Author's willful misconduct or
    gross negligence; Article 9 (2)).


Article 4. Permitted Use

You may, free of charge, do the following, except for anything that falls
under Article 6:
  (1) engage in Personal Use;
  (2) modify the Software for your own use in your own environment;
  (3) stream or post without monetization (including YouTube, X, and other social
      media);
  (4) inspect the contents of the Software within the scope of Personal Use;
  (5) Viewing and obtaining. View the Software on GitHub, and copy the Software
      in order to obtain and install it (downloading, git clone, and the like).
      You may keep the copy you obtain on your own PC, or in a private
      repository or other storage location that only you can access, and use
      it with modifications under item (2); and
  (6) Forking to make Improvement Proposals. Create a copy of the Software
      using GitHub's fork feature and use it to prepare Improvement Proposals
      and send them to the Author. Under GitHub's terms, forks of a public
      repository are public; modifications becoming public on that fork to the
      extent necessary for this purpose do not fall under Article 6 (8). You
      may not use such a fork for any purpose other than Improvement Proposals
      (Article 6 (9)).


Article 5. Use Requiring Permission

The following require the Author's PRIOR PERMISSION, given in writing or by
another recorded method (such as a direct message on X), and are PROHIBITED
without it:

  (1) Commercial Use;
  (2) Adaptation, and distribution of anything created by Adaptation;
  (3) redistribution and secondary distribution of the Software (other than
      Modified Versions), whether commercial or non-commercial;
  (4) decompilation, disassembly, and reverse engineering;
  (5) mechanically reading, extracting, or reproducing the source code, prompts,
      configuration, or other contents; and
  (6) using the contents of the Software for training machine learning models.

Items (2) and (4) through (6) do not restrict the inspection and modification
permitted under Article 4 (2), (4), and (6) (by the user, for the user's own
environment, and in preparing Improvement Proposals). In addition, the viewing,
obtaining, keeping of your own copy, and forking for Improvement Proposals
permitted under Article 4 (5) and (6) do not fall under items (3) and (5).
Business Use and publishing or distributing Modified Versions are not subject
to permission under this Article; they are prohibited by Article 6.


Article 6. Prohibited Conduct

The following are PROHIBITED in all cases. No permission under Article 7 will be
granted for them:

  (1) any act that violates applicable law or relates to criminal activity;
  (2) defaming, threatening, or discriminating against others, or otherwise
      infringing the rights or interests of others;
  (3) impersonating a real person or organization, or presenting the Software's
      output as a statement of a real person or organization;
  (4) reproducing, imitating, or synthesizing a third party's voice, likeness,
      or other identifying attributes without that party's consent;
  (5) any use that damages the value or reputation of the character Hatsune Miku
      or any other character, and any use contrary to public order and morals
      (including use contrary to the Piapro Character License and the guidelines
      of Crypton Future Media, Inc.); and
  (6) using the Software to gain unauthorized access to, place excessive load
      on, or otherwise interfere with any other system or third-party service;
  (7) Business Use;
  (8) publishing, distributing, or redistributing a Modified Version (whether
      for a fee or free of charge, including making a Modified Version
      available for third parties to obtain or use), except for showing
      modifications to the Author as an Improvement Proposal (Article 4 (6));
      and
  (9) using a fork under Article 4 (6) for any purpose other than Improvement
      Proposals (including using the fork as a place to distribute, promote,
      or publish a Modified Version, or having third parties use the Modified
      Version on the fork).

The Author's adoption of an Improvement Proposal, and the Author's publication
or distribution of the Software including it, are not restricted by this
Article (Article 2 (4) and (6)).


Article 7. Requesting Permission

For Commercial Use or any other act under Article 5, please contact the Author.
Permission is granted individually, in recorded form. Acts under Article 6
(including Business Use and publishing or distributing Modified Versions) are
