The Author's permission extends only to the Author's own rights; it does not
include any license of the rights of third parties, such as the character
Hatsune Miku, Live2D, or voice models. For those, follow the terms of the
respective rights holders (Articles 3 and 13).

  X (Twitter): https://x.com/ChordDotE


Article 8. User Responsibilities

You use the Software at your own risk and expense, and you are responsible for:

  (1) Costs. The Software uses third-party services including Google AI Studio
      (Gemini), Fish Audio, and Tavily. Their fees are payable by you under your
      contract with each provider (Article 3 (2)). Usage varies with conversation, Miku's
      autonomous activity, and music creation, and may exceed your expectations.
  (2) Credentials. Setting, storing, and updating API keys, app passwords, login
      passwords, and other credentials. These credentials, as well as
      conversations, memories, registered face photos and voice recordings, and
      other data handled by the Software, are stored unencrypted in your
      environment.
  (3) Access control. Where the Software is made reachable by others - from
      other devices on the same network, or via external publication (tunnel) -
      setting a login password and otherwise controlling access. Without it,
      anyone who can reach it may be able to access conversations, memories,
      registered faces and voices, settings, and other information handled by
      the Software. In addition, the Software can be used without a password
      from the PC on which it runs, whether or not a login password is set, so
      you are also responsible for managing that PC.
  (4) Third parties. Where microphone, camera, or other input captures a third
      party's voice, image, or personal data: informing that party and obtaining
      consent. Such input may be transmitted to third-party services.
  (5) Externally obtained material. When you ask for a cover (a reproduction
      of an existing song) in the music features, the Software automatically
      searches the internet based on the song title (giving priority to any
      URL you provide), and automatically downloads a score (MIDI) from the
      pages it finds or, if none is found, audio (such as MP3), as well as the
      text of pages that publish the lyrics. The downloaded material is saved
      in your environment (in the folder for each song) and used for
      transcribing the reference melody and referring to the lyrics. When
      downloading, the Software sends requests in the same form as an ordinary
      web browser.
      The Author has not verified, and does not warrant, the lawfulness of the
      sources or the rights in the material they publish. You shall use
      downloaded material only within the scope of private use, and should
      check the terms of the source and the conditions of the rights holders.
      If use of the material may violate the source's conditions, do not use
      it. Publication of such material or of output based on it is governed by
      item (6).
  (6) Output. Your use, storage, and publication of conversations, text, music,
      singing, audio, and other output generated by the Software. Where output
      involves third-party rights, you must obtain the necessary clearances.
  (7) Compliance with the laws applicable where you are located and where you
      use the Software.
  (8) Backing up conversations, memories, settings, and other data.


Article 9. Disclaimer and No Warranty

  (1) The Software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or
      implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
